<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="AARCH64:LE:64:v8A:default">
<!--
    MachineOutliner fragments inlined into their callers
    (`option outlinedinline on|off`, default on).

    Issue: clang's MachineOutliner moves instruction sequences that repeat
    across functions into shared `OUTLINED_FUNCTION_<n>` fragments. A fragment
    has no frame and reads and writes its caller's registers, so a caller
    printed as opaque calls: `_OUTLINED_FUNCTION_0()` with no arguments where
    the source added two parameters, and a tail call to a fragment in place of
    the `exit(7)` the fragment makes.

    Stage / sub-stage: P2 inline-inject. The analysis commit flags each
    function symbol named `OUTLINED_FUNCTION_<n>` inline
    (`p2_lift/kuna_outlinedinline.rs`), so flow splices it into the caller; the
    hard-model inliner keeps a fragment's own RETURN when the caller tail-calls
    it or nothing follows the call.

    P0 assertion: `option outlinedinline on|off`, set after `load file` and
    before the `read symbols` that commits the flags.

    The XML wrapper only supplies the harness architecture; both passes load
    the plain arm64 `macho_arm64_outlined` fixture (see the fixtures README).

    Pass 1 (off) reproduces the BUG: `_sum2` returns
    `_OUTLINED_FUNCTION_0() + 3` and `_bail` tail-calls `_OUTLINED_FUNCTION_1`.
    Pass 2 (the default) is the FIX: `_sum2` returns `(a0 + a1) * 2 + 3` and
    `_bail` calls `exit(7)`.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
c0035fd6
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/macho_arm64_outlined</com>
  <com>option outlinedinline off</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>load function _sum2</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>load function _bail</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/macho_arm64_outlined</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>load function _sum2</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>load function _bail</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="OUTLINEDINLINE #1: off calls the fragment" min="1" max="1">return _OUTLINED_FUNCTION_0\(.*\) \+ 3;</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="OUTLINEDINLINE #2: on inlines the fragment's arithmetic" min="1" max="1">return \(a0 \+ a1\) \* 2 \+ 3;</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="OUTLINEDINLINE #3: off tail-calls the fragment" min="1" max="1">_OUTLINED_FUNCTION_1\(</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="OUTLINEDINLINE #4: on inlines the tail-called fragment" min="1" max="1">exit\(7\);</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
